{% comment %}
  BW Kicker Content Block
  Braze content block: "kicker"

  Reads kicker details from the "kickers" catalog using kicker_id, which is
  assigned in the email body from the "email-content-test" catalog lookup.

  For catalog-driven emails (email-content-test):
    Required variables (assigned in email body):
      kicker_id  - ID of the kicker row in the "kickers" catalog (e.g. "seating", "outdoor")
                   If blank, the email body shows categories-images instead.

  For batch/blast emails (no catalog):
    Use if/elsif in the email body to select a pre-built kicker content block directly
    (e.g. kicker-outdoor, kicker-dining, kicker-clearance). Dynamic content block names
    via assigned variables do not work in Braze.

    {% assign kicker_id = "outdoor" %}
    {% if kicker_id == "outdoor" %}
    {{content_blocks.${kicker-outdoor} | id: 'cb3'}}
    {% elsif kicker_id == "dining" %}
    {{content_blocks.${kicker-dining} | id: 'cb3'}}
    {% elsif kicker_id == "clearance" %}
    {{content_blocks.${kicker-clearance} | id: 'cb3'}}
    {% endif %}
    Set kicker_id = "" to show no kicker.

  Catalogs:
    kickers
      id            - Kicker identifier (seating, outdoor, clearance, dining, ...)
      image_url     - Full URL of the kicker image
      url           - Click-through URL (defaults to https://www.burrow.com if blank)
      alt           - Alt text for the image

  Email body usage (catalog-driven):
    {% assign email_id = "20260426" %}
    {% catalog_items email-content-test {{ email_id }} %}
    {% assign banner_id = items[0].banner %}
    {% assign kicker_id = items[0].kicker %}
    ...
    {% if kicker_id != blank %}
    {{content_blocks.${kicker} | id: 'cb3'}}
    {% else %}
    {{content_blocks.${categories-images} | id: 'cb3'}}
    {% endif %}
{% endcomment %}

{% catalog_items kickers {{ kicker_id }} %}
{% assign kicker = items[0] %}
{% assign kicker_url = kicker.url | default: "https://www.burrow.com" %}

<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
  <tr>
    <td align="center" style="padding:0; margin:0;">
      <a href="{{ kicker_url }}">
        <img src="{{ kicker.image_url }}" alt="{{ kicker.alt }}" width="600" style="display:block; width:100%; max-width:600px; height:auto; border:0;" />
      </a>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
